    [BugFix][Attention] Fix strided MLA prefill RoPE padding and KV reads (#18798)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Fix two strided MLA PROLOG_V3 prefill regressions introduced by #18256
    and observed in the Kimi A3 nightly run:
    
    1. Slice the prefill cos/sin tables to the actual prefill token count
    before query RoPE and PROLOG_V3. Metadata can retain graph padding while
    both operator inputs contain only actual tokens. Keep the shared
    metadata unchanged.
    2. Read current KV rows with the existing stride-aware
    `copy_pcp_kv_cache` kernel instead of advanced indexing on the entire
    strided cache. Extract the existing slot padding/copy logic into a
    shared reader, retain its A3 partial-tile protection, and materialize
    only the selected rows as dense TND outputs.
    
    The second fix avoids `aclnnIndex` materializing a contiguous copy of
    the full historical cache. Temporary outputs scale with the current
    chunk size.
    
    Failure evidence:
    
    - [Kimi-K2.6-w4a8-A3: InterleaveRope batch-size
    mismatch](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38628357039/job/116076044114)
    - [Kimi long-context: RoPE mismatch and current-KV indexing
    OOM](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/38628357039/job/116076044749)
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Fixes padded prefill execution and reduces temporary memory used to read
    current KV from strided caches. No configuration changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - CPU regression and device adapter tests: **171 passed**.
      ```bash
      python -m pytest -q \
        tests/ut/attention/test_mla_prolog_v3_route.py \
        tests/ut/device/test_paged_mla_cache_read.py \
        tests/ut/device/test_device_op.py
      ```
    - RoPE coverage: pure/mixed prefill with and without graph padding;
    checks both operator tables and unchanged metadata.
    - Slot-reader coverage: FP16/BF16, component-major/token-fused layouts,
    empty/single/negative/all-negative/duplicate/out-of-order/cross-page
    slots, partial tiles, dense outputs, and unchanged source storage.
    Guards reject direct source-cache indexing or contiguous conversion.
    - `bash format.sh ci`: passed.
    - mypy 1.11.1: changed production files and changed test files each
    passed for Python 3.10, 3.11, and 3.12 with the CI-verified vLLM source.
    Full-tree errors from local dependency differences are identical to the
    unmodified main baseline; no new errors.
    - Added a real NPU regression in
    `tests/e2e/nightly/single_node/ops/singlecard_ops/triton/test_pcp_kv_cache.py::test_current_mla_kv_read_does_not_copy_history_cache`.
    It reads 8193 current rows from both layouts, checks values/negative
    slots/source preservation, and rejects peak temporary allocation
    consistent with a full 256 MiB NoPE cache copy.
    - Real NPU execution, graph capture, and end-to-end Kimi reruns remain
    pending; the local development host has no NPU.
    
